   ("Squeeze theorem and one-sided limits", ul(["If $g\\le f\\le h$ near $a$ and $g,h\\to L$, then $f\\to L$.", "Example: $-x^2\\le x^2\\sin\\frac1x\\le x^2$, so $\\lim_{x\\to0}x^2\\sin\\frac1x=0$.", "$\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{|x|}{x}$ does not exist: left limit $-1$, right limit $+1$.", "Piecewise functions: compute each one-sided limit with the matching formula."])),
